			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Correct optional field handling and type safety across services\n\nUpdate generated catalog versions to 2026-06-11. Fix optional property spreading in WorkbenchNotificationService and WorkbenchProgressService to only include defined values, preventing undefined from being sent to upstream. Resolve type errors in Workspaces event payload extraction, FileSystem IStat re-export, globalThis property access in ResolveConfiguration, Tauri IPC args typing, MistWebSocketTransport backoff array access, and TauriMainProcessService TierIPC lookup. Move fileSystemProviderService lookup outside registration loop in WorkbenchIntegration. Remove unused fileTypeToString and Install exports.\n\nImpact: Eliminates TypeScript errors, ensures proper optional field semantics for upstream compatibility, and improves code correctness across the Wind service layer.",
			"SHA": "2eb0d8a78c566a51b31621d28c3a3aed963f7ba3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T20:18:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2000,
				300
			],
			"Message": "build(Wind): Regenerate upstream service interfaces and complete bridge shape generation\n\nRestore 150+ generated service interface files under Source/Effect/Generated/ from VS Code upstream sources, adding CommandCatalog.ts with 551 command registrations and ServiceCatalog.ts with 516 service decorator entries. Reformat all ESBuild configuration files (BaseConfig, CompileConfig, TargetConfig, Wind.js, Target.js, index.js, and constants) to expanded multi-line format for readability. Add 15 Workbench*BridgeShapeGenerated.ts bridge shape files mapping upstream service interfaces to Wind's __CEL_SERVICES__ global registry, plus UserSettingsBridgeShapeGenerated.ts for configuration service bridging.\n\nImpact: Completes the codegen pipeline established in prior commits, aligns all upstream service definitions with current VS Code sources, and provides full bridge shape coverage for Wind workbench services.",
			"SHA": "7047ccd216f76ed55fa489dc84c1f5358b3775ca"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T15:20:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1150,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Wind): Update tsconfig.tsbuildinfo with new codegen output\n\nThe `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` file has been updated to reflect the latest generated service interfaces and bridge shapes. This includes:\n- CommandCatalog.ts with 551 command registrations\n- ServiceCatalog.ts with 516 service decorator entries\n- 15 Workbench*BridgeShapeGenerated.ts files for service bridging\n- Telemetry service layer updates for synchronous initialization\n\nImpact: Ensures accurate type checking and compilation of generated TypeScript interfaces.",
			"SHA": "49c3e07d12535b55bf2070c9e6731228af8271b7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T15:20:15Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1150,
				120
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Implement codegen pipeline for upstream service interfaces\n\nAdd new codegen pipeline that extracts service interfaces from VS Code upstream sources and generates Wind-compatible bridge shapes. The pipeline consists of:\n\n- Lightweight regex-based extractors for `createDecorator` calls and interface members (`ExtractDecoratorMatch`, `ExtractInterfaceMembers`)\n- Cross-file interface resolver for decorators referencing external interfaces (`ResolveInterfaceCrossFile`)\n- Strongly-typed records for codegen errors (`CodegenProblem`) and interface members (`InterfaceMemberRecord`)\n- Async filesystem walker for the VS Code source tree (`SourceTreeWalker`)\n\nThe generated service interfaces are now consumed by Wind to create bridge shapes that mirror upstream verbatim. This enables precise effectful bridging between the workbench services and the Tauri backend.\n\nImpact: Enables regeneration of all upstream service interfaces and establishes the foundation for schema-driven bridge generation.",
			"SHA": "f35670789689d68ef685b008ebec2aff2fdd41b8"
		},
